The  command is a server which supports OMRON LUNA’s network boot
protocol based on the Transparent Remote File System (TRFS)  pro‐
tocol.   The TRFS protocol uses special Ethernet type packets and
works within a local network.  is a simple TRFS server that  only
supports  client  reads for booting and exports files in a speci‐
fied directory.  accepts requests only from clients listed in the
and have valid hostnames.  The options are as follows: Run in de‐
bug mode with specified tracelevel.  The tracelevel can be  value
1,  2,  or 3, and greater tracelevel provides more detailed trace
output.  The server will not fork in the debug mode.   Specify  a
network  interface  to  service  network  boot.  If not specified
searches available network interfaces  (excluding  loopback)  and
use  the  first  configured  one.  Specify a directory containing
boot files to be served by If not specified uses by default.   is
